  "chunk": "mistakes across multiple game sessions. These patterns point to a fundamental\ndistinction between pattern matching and genuine understanding. The models\ncan generate fluent, seemingly reasonable explanations of their actions, but these\nexplanations often contradict their actual behaviour.\nOur findings align with Mitchell’s warning about the “first-step fallacy”,\nmistaking achievements in specific domains for progress toward general intel-\nligence. While LLMs demonstrate impressive capabilities in many domains,\ntheir failure atZorkreveals the current limitations of LLMs. These are likely\nnot quantitative limitations that might be resolved with larger models or more\ntraining data, but potentially a qualitative difference in how these systems pro-\ncess information versus how humans understand and reason about the world.\nOn the other hand, one might argue whether human-like understanding and\nreasoning is even a necessary condition toward general intelligence or whether",
